/**
@defgroup core Core
@brief Application and main loop, window, keyboard/mouse/gamepad input, action mapping, events,
signals, fixed timestep, logging, assertions and a scoped CPU profiler.

The lowest engine layer. Everything else builds on it, and it depends only on GLFW, OpenGL (through
GLAD) and spdlog. See @ref core_guide for an explanation of how the pieces work together.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/core/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup renderer Renderer
@brief 2D camera (rotation, parallax, shake), batched quad, sprite and text rendering, sprite
sheets and animation, render targets and post-processing, OpenGL wrappers.

Builds on @ref core. The camera, sprite sheet layout and animation player do not use OpenGL and
are unit-tested; Renderer2D and the wrappers need a current OpenGL 3.3 context. See
@ref renderer_guide for how batching works and how the pieces fit together.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/renderer/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup assets Assets
@brief Loading each texture, shader and font file once, with hot reloading.

Builds on @ref renderer. See the asset cache section of @ref renderer_guide.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/assets/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup audio Audio
@brief Sound effects and music: decoding, overlapping voices with volume, pitch and pan, effect
and music buses, and a mode without an output device for tests and headless machines.

Depends only on @ref core (logging, assertions) and the vendored miniaudio; no OpenGL. See
@ref audio_guide.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/audio/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup ecs ECS
@brief Entities with generations, sparse-set component storage, the Registry, views and
component signals.

Depends only on @ref core (assertions); no OpenGL, so all of it is unit-tested. See
@ref ecs_guide for how sparse sets and views work and the rules for changing the registry while
iterating.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/ecs/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup physics Physics
@brief Rigid bodies, circle/box/polygon shapes, broad phases (brute force, sort and sweep, uniform
grid), narrow phase with contact manifolds, an impulse solver with friction and restitution,
triggers, one-way platforms, sleeping, continuous collision and tile map collision.

Depends only on @ref core (assertions) and GLM; no OpenGL and no ECS, so all of it is unit-tested.
See @ref physics_guide for how a step works and why.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/physics/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup scene Scene
@brief Scene with systems in a fixed order, built-in components (Transform, SpriteRenderer,
Animator, RigidBody, Collider, TilemapCollider), parent/child hierarchy, rendering, physics
integration (PhysicsSystem), JSON scene files and Tiled map loading.

Builds on @ref ecs, @ref physics, @ref renderer and @ref assets. See @ref ecs_guide,
@ref physics_guide and, for Tiled maps, @ref platformer_guide.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/scene/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup debug Debug tools
@brief Physics debug view (shapes, body states, bounding boxes, contacts, velocities), frame
statistics (FPS, frame times, draw calls), and a Dear ImGui overlay with a frame graph, the CPU
profiler's call tree and an entity inspector.

Builds on @ref physics, @ref renderer and @ref scene. The debug view is collected as plain lines
before it is drawn, FrameStats and FrameHistory are pure arithmetic, and the overlay's widgets run
in a headless ImGui context, so all of them are unit-tested. See @ref debug_guide.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/debug/`.
*/

/**
@namespace astra2d
@brief All public engine types and functions.

Implementation details live in `astra2d::detail` and are not part of the API.
*/
